  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 22d0308a90dc49ae97395f1b651723b5, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_TECH_01_FalsePositives
  questionId: TECH-01
  category: 1
  speakerName: Principal Security Architect
  questionText: >-
    During a technical workshop, the customer challenges your detection claims and asks how you reduce false positives without hiding real incidents. What do you do?
  answerOptions:
  - {fileID: 11400001}
  - {fileID: 11400002}
  - {fileID: 11400003}
  - {fileID: 11400004}
--- !u!114 &11400001
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d521c6b84db4b8fae30e3785d9e9582, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_TECH_01_A1
  answerText: >-
    Describe the tuning model, then ask for sample alert categories so you can test the claim against their environment.
  technicalDelta: 3
  commercialDelta: 1
  rapportDelta: 0
  energyDelta: 1
--- !u!114 &11400002
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d521c6b84db4b8fae30e3785d9e9582, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_TECH_01_A2
  answerText: >-
    Say the product uses AI and shift quickly into the roadmap.
  technicalDelta: -1
  commercialDelta: 1
  rapportDelta: -1
  energyDelta: 0
--- !u!114 &11400003
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d521c6b84db4b8fae30e3785d9e9582, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_TECH_01_A3
  answerText: >-
    Acknowledge the risk, explain the validation path, and define what evidence would make them comfortable.
  technicalDelta: 3
  commercialDelta: 0
  rapportDelta: 1
  energyDelta: -1
--- !u!114 &11400004
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d521c6b84db4b8fae30e3785d9e9582, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_TECH_01_A4
  answerText: >-
    Offer to bring in engineering later and move back to the slide deck.
  technicalDelta: 0
  commercialDelta: 0
  rapportDelta: 0
  energyDelta: -1
